# Lab Engine Rules

- Lab orchestration is QuantaHub-owned and independent from CTFd internals.
- Use runtime-provider interfaces. Do not leak Docker-specific assumptions into domain APIs.
- Supported conceptual operations: provision/start/health/reset/stop/destroy.
- Model labs as multi-service topologies, not only single containers.
- Every session has an explicit state machine and TTL.
- Provisioning is asynchronous.
- State transitions must be idempotent or safely retryable.
- Cleanup is deterministic and includes runtime workloads, networks, ephemeral volumes/state, routes, DNS/gateway records, credentials/tokens and resource reservations.
- Maintain an orphan reaper/reconciliation process.
- Capacity decisions are based primarily on active sessions and resource profiles, not registered-user count.
- Validate every published lab against the canonical Lab Manifest schema.
